GNU Coreutils FreeBASIC port
File: fb_port/README

This directory holds the FreeBASIC translation work, support declarations,
conversion driver, focused checks, and the vendored C2FB converter. The
repository contains no Coreutils implementation C sources. Keep a separate
Coreutils 9.12 source checkout to rebuild the C reference, regenerate
translations, or run the upstream suite.

Configure paths from the repository root:

  export COREUTILS_SOURCE=/path/to/coreutils-9.12
  export COREUTILS_FBC=/path/to/fbc

Then run:

  python3 fb_port/port.py reference --jobs=8
  python3 fb_port/port.py reference-tests --jobs=8
  python3 fb_port/port.py translate --contexts --jobs=8
  python3 fb_port/port.py audit --contexts
  python3 fb_port/check.py

The reference build and upstream tests use the external checkout selected by
COREUTILS_SOURCE. Translation uses the checked-in converter under
`tools/c2fb` unless COREUTILS_C2FB_TOOLS selects another checkout. The
`compiler` action also builds FreeBASIC from source and requires
COREUTILS_FBC_SOURCE. COREUTILS_FBC_INCLUDE and
COREUTILS_FBC_RUNTIME_LIBDIR can select nonstandard installation paths.

`generated-context/` contains the audited production candidate set. Each
`*_candidates.bas` body has a matching `*_candidates_types.bi` declaration
file. `candidate-map.csv` maps those pairs to relative Coreutils source paths.
The generated files are translations, not proof that each Coreutils command
is complete. The audit compares the FreeBASIC objects with the C reference;
command-level checks use hybrid executables that still link C support code.

The latest recorded status is in `STATUS.md`. Work files and logs are written
under `build/` and `logs/`; temporary reports are written under `build/`.
These outputs are ignored by Git.

end of fb_port/README
